Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:15.00,Small,,0,0,0,,Elder fraud now costs families over ten billion dollars a year. Threats. Fake arrests. Stolen passwords. In Vadodara, one family decided to fight back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.00,0:00:24.55,Small,,0,0,0,,Beta, a bank message came. They want my OTP. What do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.55,0:00:34.39,Small,,0,0,0,,Ruko, Dadaji. Do nothing. Look, the phone never even buzzed. Kavach locked the scam away before you could touch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.39,0:00:50.09,Small,,0,0,0,,See? Every reason cited. Asked for OTP. Threatened arrest. Fake urgency. I blocked the number from my office. When they called back, the phone killed it before the first ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.09,0:01:04.06,Small,,0,0,0,,And it learns. Signed rules, fresh this morning, verified on the phone itself. One family's block now protects every family. Hashes only. Never phone numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.06,0:01:13.42,Small,,0,0,0,,The server? It holds nothing but noise. Ciphertext and hashes. There is nothing here worth stealing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.42,0:01:26.91,Small,,0,0,0,,Protection for dadaji. Peace for papa. Kavach, built by thirteen year old Krishiv Joshi of Vadodara. Open source. MIT licensed.
